# [[again]], returning to the beginning (whence {{m|da|ommer}}, {{m|da|om igen}}, {{m|da|tro om igen}})
#* {{quote-book|da|year=2014|author=w:Dennis Jürgensen|title=Måske|publisher=Tellerup A/S|isbn=9788758814599
|passage=„Nej. Hvis du tror jeg vil se passivt til, mens du ødelægger din mands og dit eget liv med dette martyrium, så må du tro om ...“
|t="No. If you think I intend to look on passively while you destroy your husband's and your own life with this martyrium, you will have to think '''again''' ..."}}
#* {{quote-book|da|year=2016|author=Terje Nordberg|title=Det må godt føles rart|publisher=Lindhardt og Ringhof|isbn=9788711586600
|passage=Jo, jeg har da haft mine nu&#39;er, men hvis jeg skulle gøre det hele om, ville jeg sørge for at have mange flere af dem.
|t=Sure, I have had my nows, but if I had to do it all '''again''', I would make sure to have many more of them.}}
#* {{quote-book|da|year=2017|author=Morten Sabroe|title=Love Me Do|publisher=Politikens Forlag|isbn=9788740026726
|passage=Han skrev den '''om''' tre gange.
|t=He '''re'''wrote it three times.}}
# such that something is changed (whence {{m|da|lave om}}
#* '''2017''', Sacha Batthyany (Translated by Uffe Gardel), ''Og hvad har det med mig at gøre'', Art People {{ISBN|9788771599206}}
#*: {{quote|da|Men verdenskrisen i 1929 lukkede fabrikken, og indenrigsministeriet overtog den og byggede den '''om''' til et fængsel.
|translation=But the world crisis in 1929 closed down the factory, and the ministry of internal affairs took it and '''re'''built it into a prison.}}
# going forwards in a book or similar, [[reach]]ing some page
#* {{quote-book|da|year=2014|author=Lene Dybdahl|title=Nøglens Vogtere #2: Visigotens Hjelm|publisher=Tellerup A/S|isbn=9788758812564
|passage=Consuela bladrede langsomt '''om''' på indholdsfortegnelsen.
|t=Slowly, Consuela turned the pages till she reached the table of contents.}}
# such that something [[rotate]]s or [[revolve]]s (either of its own accord or by external influence)
